{#-
  "only when PHYSICALLY operated" / "only when PROGRAMMATICALLY operated".

  webCoRE asks whether a PERSON touched the device. Home Assistant cannot
  answer that directly -- a Hubitat hub knows, and tags its own events
  [physical] or [digital], but that tag does not survive the bridge: measured
  2026-08-16, no HA event type, no attribute, nothing across 1306 entities.

  What HA CAN answer is who caused the change, and that is enough. Every state
  change carries a context; an automation stamps its own on everything it does,
  and that context survives the bridge intact -- verified on a real
  Hubitat-bridged dimmer, where all 8 changes were attributed to the PistonCore
  automation that made them. A physical press arrives with no context at all
  (verified on a real bridged Zooz dimmer, paddle pressed by hand).

  So:
    parent_id  set   -> an automation or script did it (ours or someone else's)
    user_id    set   -> a person acting THROUGH Home Assistant: the app, the
                        dashboard, a voice assistant, an API call
    neither set -> the change came from the device itself, which is a human at
                        the switch

  DIVERGENCE, deliberate and documented: webCoRE's "physically" means the
  device's own driver reported a physical operation. This means "not through
  Home Assistant". They agree on the cases pistons actually care about, and
  differ for a device operated by some other system entirely. See
  HA_LIMITATIONS.md.

  EDIT THIS FILE if your setup needs a different rule -- for instance to treat
  a specific automation as "physical" because it mirrors a real switch. It is
  the whole reason the expression is not buried in Python.

  Variables: `physical` (true for p:"p", false for p:"s"), `trigger_var`
  (the Jinja name holding the triggering state, normally `trigger.to_state`).
-#}
{% if physical -%}
{{ trigger_var }}.context.parent_id is none and {{ trigger_var }}.context.user_id is none
{%- else -%}
not ({{ trigger_var }}.context.parent_id is none and {{ trigger_var }}.context.user_id is none)
{%- endif %}
